  "title": "FDA Recall Raises Concerns Over Glass Particles in Dog and Horse Joint Injections",
  "summary": "Pet owners and veterinarians are being urged to check their supplies after a nationwide recall involving certain lots of injectable medications used to treat joint problems in dogs and horses. The U.S. Food and Drug Administration has announced that American Regent, Inc. is recalling four lots of its Adequan products after testing identified glass fibers in internally retained samples. The recalled medications include Adequan Canine Injection, which is prescribed for dogs, and Adequan i.m. Inje",
